  "chapter": {
    "number": 33,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(34) A Psalm of David, when he changed his countenance before Abimelech; and he let him go, and he departed."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will bless the Lord at all times: his praise shall be continually in my mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My soul shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 61
          },
          {
            "text": "boast herself in the Lord: let the meek hear, and rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Magnify you⌃ the Lord with me, and let us exalt his name together.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I sought the Lord diligently, and he listened to me, and delivered me from all my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 62
          },
          {
            "text": "sojournings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Draw near to him, and be enlightened: and your faces shall not by any means be ashamed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "This poor man cried, and the Lord listened to him, and delivered him out of all his afflictions.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The angel of the Lord will encamp round about them that fear him, and will deliver them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Taste and see that the Lord is good: blessed is the man who hopes in him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fear the Lord, all you⌃ his saints: for there is no lack to them that fear him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The rich have become poor and hungry: but they that seek the Lord diligently shall not lack any good thing. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Come, you⌃ children, hear me: I will teach you the fear of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What man is there that desires life, loving to see good days?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep your tongue from evil, and your lips from speaking guile.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn away from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The eyes of the Lord are over the righteous, and his ears are open to their prayer:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "but the face of the Lord is against them that do evil, to destroy their memorial from the earth. The righteous cried, and the Lord listened to them,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and delivered them out of all their afflictions.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is near to",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 63
          },
          {
            "text": "them that are of a contrite heart; and will save the lowly in spirit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but out of them all Lord will deliver them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He keeps all their bones: not one of them shall be broken.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The death of sinners is evil: and they that hate righteousness will go wrong.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord will redeem the souls of his servants: and none of those that hope in him shall go wrong.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 61,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. be praised.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 33,
          "verse": 2
